<title>UK: AGF Braseg sets $50 mln eight-year step-up bond.</title>
<headline>AGF Braseg sets $50 mln eight-year step-up bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Societe Generale.</p>
<p> BORROWER   AGF BRASEG</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  AGF DO BRASIL</p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 COUPON     *8.125    MATURITY  **10.MAR.05</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.25    PAY DATE    10.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.60	REOFFER    100.25    SPREAD	+205 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *TO YEAR THREE, 9.0 PCT YEARS FOUR AND FIVE, 9.50 PCT</p>
<p>		TO MATURITY</p>
<p>	    **CALL AND PUT YEARS THREE AND FOUR AT PAR</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/BR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC   0.225</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND THREE-YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
